# T. Zaslavsky, "Biased Graphs. I" (1989)

Bibliography label: Zaslavsky 1989.

Published source: T. Zaslavsky, *Biased graphs. I. Bias, balance, and gains*,
Journal of Combinatorial Theory, Series B 47(1) (1989), 32--52.
DOI: `10.1016/0095-8956(89)90063-4`.

For a classical gain graph, reversing an edge inverts its group-valued gain;
a circle is balanced when its gain product is the identity. Switching changes
edge gains by vertex labels. This vocabulary applies directly to the
invertible group-labelled layer of directed transport. General one-way monoid
labels and max-affine floor maps lie outside the classical gain-graph object.

This file is a source-positioning note. It states no Lean version of the
paper's biased-graph or matroid results.
